      "writtenOn": "2018-07-11T23:52:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "GPIO_INT_BOTH is defined as GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_INT_F_FALLING | GPIO_INT_F_RISING. NPCX code relies on GPIO_INT_F_{FALLING/RISING} to decide if PSL_IN should be configured for edge trigger or not. So, even though this pin is not being used as an interrupt doing normal operations, we need to set interrupt flags just to allow NPCX code to do the right thing. I mentioned GPIO_INPUT on purpose above to indicate that this is acting as a normal input pin during EC operation.\n\nIf it makes things more clear I can add flags: GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_INT_BOTH | GPIO_HIB_WAKE_HIGH even though it is redundant.",
